ORDINANCE IV OF 1995
ORDINANCE IV OF 1995
NORTH‑WEST FRONTIER PROVINCE HEALTH FOUNDATION ORDINANCE, 1995
2. Definitions.‑‑In
this Ordinance, unless the context otherwise requires, the following
expressions shall have the meanings hereby respectively assigned to them, that is
to say‑‑‑
(a) "Board" means the Board of Directors
constituted under section 4;
(b) "Chairman" means the Chairman of the
Board;
(c) "Committee" means
a Director of the Board and includes the Chairman;
(d) "Director" means a Director of the
Board and includes the Chairman;
(e) "Foundation" means the North‑West
Frontier Province Health Foundation establishment under section 3;
(f) "Government" means the Government of
the North‑West Frontier Province;
(g) "Governor" means the Governor of the
North‑West Frontier Province;
(h) "local body" means a Local Council
constituted under the North -West Frontier Province Local Government Ordinance,
1979 (N.‑W.F.P. Ordinance IV of 1979);
(i) "Managing
Director" means the Managing Director of the Foundation appointed under
section 6;
(j) "NGO" means Non‑Governmental
Organization, duly registered with the Government, offering health services;
(k) "prescribed"
means prescribed by rules made under this Ordinance;
(I) "Provincial
Assembly" means the Provincial Assembly of the North West Frontier
Province;
(m) "section" means a
section of this Ordinance; and
(n) "Vice‑Chairman"
means the Vice‑Chairman of the Board.
